saphira-llm is an independently authored C11 inference runtime for BitNet
1.58-bit and conventional GGUF models, targeting x86-64-v3 on Saphira Linux.

No third-party source code is vendored into this distribution. Upstream
projects are consulted as engineering references and are recorded by exact
revision and licence in PROVENANCE.md. Where behaviour is reproduced, the
algorithm has been independently reimplemented in C from the documented
behaviour of those references; no source has been copied.

Any future inclusion of third-party source must be recorded in PROVENANCE.md
and NOTICE before it is committed, and must be licence-compatible with the
MIT terms in LICENSE.
